A||||6||Punkndrublic||Alternators
Z||000000||Punkndrublic||06-02-99||09:37 PM||||Anyone now of high amp alternator that puts out more amps then the stock? and won't empty my wallet. And if i were to increase the size of the pulley on the stock one to make it spin faster would it wreck it or something in the electrical system.
Z||000001||Phil||06-03-99||04:40 AM||||A larger pully on the alt will make it spin slower
Z||000002||theogre||06-03-99||12:09 PM||||any standard GM alternator should work. You can find some huge outputs in cadilac, or any other large GM cars or trucks. Those will taske you to 100-120 amps at least. Look for some trashed caddy with power everything + AC.<p>getting higher output than that is going to likely require an aftermarket unit. 
Z||000003||lowCG||06-03-99||02:01 PM||||A mail order place (J.C.Whitney)  had offered some upgrade/rebuild kits that gave 100-120amps for a very low price($20-$40),you might check there.Spinning an alternator harder won't give any advantages,with a generator it would(have),but not too many cars in the world use these anymore.If you don't feel comfortable taking apart your daily transpo ,I'd go to the junkyard.If you do this,keep in mind that there are several differences between alternators in different cars(location of attachment points,pulley,plugs)so you might want to take it along for a perfect match.
Z||000004||GREENDANO||06-03-99||04:08 PM||||All the alternators that are the style that go on the Fiero can be disassembled and the rear part rotated so the plug is orientated correctly.  The new Alt. I got for my GT needed to be rotated 180 degrees.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000005||PaUL||06-04-99||02:08 AM||||the alternators used in the fieros were the 12SI delcos. Theres plenty of sources to get a higher output one. The 12SI is similar to the older 10SI and are interchangeable expcept for the metric threads on the 12SI. The 10SI has a metal fan as opposed to a round plastic one on the 12si. Both types have an internal voltage regulator. Luckily these are much cheaper than the newer alts GM is using these days. Ive seen a site selling high amp models for around $30, i wish i could find the link.
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||06-04-99||02:18 AM||||These are the codes for the Fiero alternators<br>code        ampere<br>K22         94<br>K81         66<br>K99         85<br>K69         100                     <br>One of these codes should be located under the front hood on the drivers side fender.
